# Section Picker Menu Revamp

## Context

The custom-page section picker is a narrow absolute dropdown whose category
metadata, discovery controls, and hierarchy no longer match the rest of the
builder. Only one category currently explains what it contains.

## Goal

- Replace the dropdown with a responsive, accessible section-picker dialog.
- Add search, an optional compact view, intentional category/type iconography,
  and complete descriptions for every category and registered section type.
- Preserve insertion position, clipboard paste behavior, and the authoritative
  `pages.content` section contract.

## Non-Goals

- Do not change stored page data, backend APIs, renderer behavior, or section
  availability.
- Do not add drag-and-drop behavior to the picker.

## Steps

1. Centralize complete frontend picker metadata for the 20 registered types and
   five categories.
2. Build the responsive searchable dialog and retain add/paste semantics.
3. Add focused interaction, metadata, accessibility, and responsive coverage.
4. Run frontend tests, lint, TypeScript/build, policy, todo, and diff checks.

## Verification

- Focused `BlockRenderer` tests and complete frontend tests.
- Frontend lint, TypeScript/production build, native-dialog, managed-form,
  loading-boundary, and media-placeholder checks.
- Todo pairing/status and `git diff --check`.

